<http://data.silknow.org/object/bbcf5f33-8562-3505-ba57-0f1d30175b52>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Textile sample of Jacquard woven figured silk in pale blue and white with a floral design repeated five times in the width of the fabric. The design consists of leaves and stems and daisy-like flowers, and some of the flowers are displayed against the centre of the largest leaf. There is an exact repeat of the design with a plain band at the top and bottom.\n\nThe selvedges are woven in plain tabby 0.19 inch wide with a red outer stripe. There is a small paper stuck to the right-hand side."@en , "Textile sample of Jacquard woven figured silk, possibly made in England or France, ca. 1840-1860"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/e3a2cb92-1371-3d6a-9104-f58b2a4aace0> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Textile sample of Jacquard woven figured silk in pale blue and white with a floral design repeated five times in the width of the fabric. The design consists of leaves and stems and daisy-like flowers, and some of the flowers are displayed against the centre of the largest leaf. There is an exact repeat of the design with a plain band at the top and bottom.\n\nThe selvedges are woven in plain tabby 0.19 inch wide with a red outer stripe. There is a small paper stuck to the right-hand side."@en , "Textile sample of Jacquard woven figured silk, possibly made in England or France, ca. 1840-1860"@en ;
